@SyncForge.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5279

### Verificar se a aplicação está respondendo

GET {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: text/plain

### Cadastrar um contato

POST {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": " Pedro.Http@Example.com ",
  "firstName": " Pedro ",
  "lastName": " Silva ",
  "phone": "11999999999"
}

### Tentar cadastrar o mesmo e-mail normalizado

POST {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "pedro.http@example.com",
  "firstName": "Outro nome",
  "lastName": "Silva",
  "phone": "11888888888"
}

### Enviar um e-mail inválido

POST {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "email-invalido",
  "firstName": "Pedro"
}

### Enviar um e-mail vazio

POST {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "firstName": "Pedro"
}

### Enviar JSON malformado de propósito

POST {{SyncForge.Api_HostAddress}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email":
}

###